# BSan gate of libavutil/formats wave 1 at 0a2fbf9bb7 — FAILED (timeouts, equiv and ub_safe)

Gate: clippy, plain, asan-ubsan, tsan, bsan lib (501) and ub_unsafe (72) pass. `bsan` equiv and
ub_safe hit the gate's 7200 s timeout (exit 124); at wave 0 they took 13m26s and 24m26s.
No BSan "Undefined Behavior" report was printed by either.
Command: BSAN_OPTIONS=gc_hang_threshold_ms=600000 CRUSTIFY_FFMPEG_VARIANT=bsan timeout 7200 cargo bsan test --test <equiv|ub_safe> -- --skip compile_fail

Orchestrator triage — each test alone, same binaries, 1500 s cap, peak RSS:
| binary | test | result |
|---|---|---|
| ub_safe | samplefmt::buffers::many_planar_channels_spill_the_plane_pointers | timeout, 62 GB |
| equiv | imgutils::images::copies_and_fills_match_c_for_every_format | timeout, 14 GB |
| equiv | imgutils::images::allocations_match_c | timeout, 4.4 GB |
| ub_safe | samplefmt::buffers::every_owner_and_view_stays_inside_its_planes | timeout, 3.8 GB |
| ub_safe | imgutils::images::exact_planes_of_every_format_copy_and_fill | ok in 867 s, 282 MB |
| ub_safe | csp::cie_xy::heap_box_owner_lives_reads_writes_clones_and_frees | ok in 6 s |
| ub_safe | bprint::fields::a_string_read_outlives_the_handle | ok in 6 s |
| ub_safe | samplefmt:: minus samplefmt::buffers (12 tests) | ok in 6 s |
| equiv | imgutils:: minus imgutils::images | ok in 6 s |
These match the runtime's known cost profile (per-retag cost growing with a long-lived allocation's
history; runaway after Rust slice views of multi-KiB C blocks): see the shared test recipes' BSan section.
The gate cannot judge the affected tests' UB verdict under BSan until they finish. Promotion is
blocked until the reviewed wave passes the BSan gate within its timeout.

